# DSL & Styling

## Element Macros

### box

Flexbox container for layout. Supports borders, backgrounds, and all flex properties.

```elixir
box padding: 2, border: :single do
  text do: "Hello"
end
```

### text

Styled text content. Children are plain strings.

```elixir
text color: :cyan, bold: true do
  "Hello, world!"
end
```

### input

Raw input field.

```elixir
input placeholder: "Type..."
```

### button

Clickable action element.

```elixir
button padding_h: 1, border: :rounded do
  text do: "Submit"
end
```

### grid / col

Grid container and column children.

```elixir
grid do
  col flex: 1 do
    text do: "Left"
  end
  col flex: 2 do
    text do: "Right (wider)"
  end
end
```

### live_component

Stateful child component. Requires `id` for lifecycle reconciliation.

```elixir
live_component(Counter, id: "main", initial_count: 5)
```

## Flex Layout {: .col-2}

### Direction & Wrapping

```elixir
flex_direction: :row       # default
flex_direction: :column

flex_wrap: :no_wrap         # default
flex_wrap: :wrap
```

### Growth & Shrinking

```elixir
flex_grow: 0.0              # default
flex_shrink: 1.0            # default
flex_basis: :auto           # default, or a float

# Shorthand — flex: N expands to:
#   flex_grow: N, flex_shrink: 1.0, flex_basis: 0.0
flex: 1
```

### Justify Content (main axis)

```elixir
justify_content: :flex_start    # default
justify_content: :flex_end
justify_content: :center
justify_content: :space_between
justify_content: :space_around
justify_content: :space_evenly
```

### Align Items (cross axis)

```elixir
align_items: :stretch       # default
align_items: :flex_start
align_items: :flex_end
align_items: :center
align_items: :baseline
```

### Align Self (child override)

```elixir
align_self: :auto           # default (inherits align_items)
align_self: :flex_start
align_self: :flex_end
align_self: :center
align_self: :stretch
align_self: :baseline
```

### Align Content (wrapped lines)

```elixir
align_content: :stretch       # default
align_content: :flex_start
align_content: :flex_end
align_content: :center
align_content: :space_between
align_content: :space_around
```

## Sizing & Spacing {: .col-2}

### Dimensions

```elixir
width: 40
height: 10
min_width: 20
min_height: 5
max_width: 80
max_height: 24
```

All accept a float or `nil` (unconstrained, the default).

### Padding

```elixir
padding: 2                  # all sides
padding_h: 1                # left + right
padding_v: 1                # top + bottom
padding_left: 1             # individual sides
padding_right: 1
padding_top: 1
padding_bottom: 1
```

### Margin

```elixir
margin: 1                   # all sides
margin_left: 1              # individual sides
margin_right: 1
margin_top: 1
margin_bottom: 1
```

### Gap

```elixir
gap: 1                      # both axes
gap_main: 1                 # main axis only
gap_cross: 1                # cross axis only
```

## Borders & Overflow {: .col-2}

### Border Styles

```elixir
border: :single    # ┌ ─ ┐ │ └ ┘
border: :double    # ╔ ═ ╗ ║ ╚ ╝
border: :rounded   # ╭ ─ ╮ │ ╰ ╯

border_color: :cyan
```

Borders create a 1-cell inset on each side, reducing inner content space.

### Text Overflow

```elixir
overflow: :visible          # default — content can exceed bounds
overflow: :hidden           # clip content to inner bounds
overflow: :scroll           # clip + shift by scroll_offset

white_space: :normal        # default — text wraps
white_space: :nowrap        # prevent wrapping

overflow_wrap: :normal      # default
overflow_wrap: :break_word  # break long words

text_overflow: :clip        # default
text_overflow: :ellipsis    # show "…" at truncation point
```

## Text Styling {: .col-2}

### Text Decorations

```elixir
bold: true
dim: true
italic: true
strikethrough: true
overline: true
reverse: true               # swap fg/bg
hidden: true                # conceal text
blink: true
```

### Underline

```elixir
underline: true             # straight underline

underline_style: :straight  # or :double, :curly,
                            #    :dotted, :dashed, :none
underline_color: :red       # independent underline color
```

## Colors {: .col-2}

### Named Colors

```elixir
# Basic 8
:black  :red      :green    :yellow
:blue   :magenta  :cyan     :white

# Bright variants
:bright_black    :bright_red
:bright_green    :bright_yellow
:bright_blue     :bright_magenta
:bright_cyan     :bright_white

# Aliases
:dark_gray       # = :bright_black
:light_gray      # = :white
:default         # reset to terminal default
```

### 256-Color & RGB

```elixir
# 256-color palette (0–255)
color: 196                  # bright red
bg: 21                      # bright blue

# Truecolor RGB tuple
color: {255, 0, 128}
bg: {64, 64, 200}
```

### Color Props

Colors work on these props:

- `color` (or `fg`) — text foreground
- `bg` — background fill
- `border_color` — border foreground
- `underline_color` — underline color

### Theme Tokens

```elixir
# Default theme tokens
:bg        # :black
:fg        # :white
:primary   # :blue
:secondary # :cyan
:success   # :green
:warning   # :yellow
:danger    # :red
:muted     # :bright_black
:border    # :white
:surface   # :bright_black
```

Use in components:

```elixir
color = theme(assigns, :primary)
```

## Built-in Components {: .col-2}

### divider

```elixir
import Courgette.Components

divider(orientation: :horizontal)
divider(orientation: :vertical, color: :cyan)
```

### badge

```elixir
badge(label: "OK", color: :green)
badge(label: "Error", color: :red)
```

### heading

```elixir
heading(text: "Dashboard")
heading(text: "Status", color: :cyan, divider: false)
```

### key_value

```elixir
key_value(label: "Name", value: "Jeff")
```

### empty_state

```elixir
empty_state(message: "No items found")
```
